laurel 2303: CPU frequency governor on the SM6125 OSM + TSENS thermal caps (new bsd/dev/laurel_thermal.c; negroni 0280/0283/0284 ideas on trinket hardware). One 100 ms kernel thread: busy % per cluster (processor_cpu_load_info, busiest core over 300 ms) steps the OSM row of Silver (pwrcl 0xf521000) and Gold (perfcl 0xf523000) between the ABL row (floor) and the cap; every 1 s TSENS (0x4411000, sensors 6-12 CPU, 15 GPU) reads -40..125 C and ignores a single sensor > 20 C above the others, lowers the Gold cap at >= 95 C (down to row 0, below the ABL floor of the governor) (Silver too at >= 105 C) and raises it again below 85 C. Replaces the topaz 0094 pin of Gold at max (kept as the fallback when the governor is off). Lines 'LAUREL CPUFREQ: on: OSM governor, silver rows ..' / 'off: ..', 'LAUREL THERMAL: on: TSENS cpu N C gpu N C ..' / 'off: ..', a status line a minute and on cap changes. Kill switches laurelcpugov=0, laurelthermal=0.

